,{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfons","key":"kemperpau","last":"Kemper","name":"Kemper, Alfons","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18420/btw2025-14","pages":"281-308","publisher":"Gesellschaft für Informatik","status":"p","title":"Datenbanksysteme für Business, Technologie und Web (BTW 2025)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dfa9cfd9-7a01-4821-b9c0-78cfcfeb1745"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhancing In-Memory Spatial Indexing with Learned Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798564","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The rate at which applications gather geospatial data today has turned data loading into a critical component of data analysis pipelines. However, users are confronted with multiple file formats for storing geospatial data and an array of systems for processing it. To shed light on how the choice of file format and system affects performance, this paper explores the performance of loading geospatial data stored in diverse file formats using different libraries. It aims to study the impact of different file formats, compare loading throughput across spatial libraries, and examine the microarchitectural behavior of geospatial data loading. Our findings show that GeoParquet files provide the highest loading throughput across all benchmarked libraries. Furthermore, we note that the more spatial features per byte a file format can store, the higher the data loading throughput. Our micro-architectural analysis reveals high instructions per cycle (IPC) during spatial data loading for most libraries and formats. Additionally, our experiments show that instruction misses dominate L1 cache misses, except for GeoParquet files, where data misses take over.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wachs, Aske","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747270"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Geographic Information Systems","Micro architectural analysis","database performance evaluation","spatial libraries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of geospatial data loading","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3662165.3662761","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747270","identifier":[{"id":"85197277517","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f98de618-8764-44a0-880b-dd6b8a904179"],"keyword":["benchmarking","database performance evaluation","geographic information systems","micro-architectural analysis","spatial libraries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1076DE8329EB8D84FB028419DB7F5E40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3662165.3662761","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105371530/dbtest24-final1-TziritaZacharatou.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Aske","key":"wachspau","last":"Wachs","name":"Wachs, Aske","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3662165.3662761","eisbn":["9798400706691"],"isbn":["9798400706691"],"pages":"36-42","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DBTest '24: Proceedings of the Tenth International Workshop on Testing Database Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197277517"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f98de618-8764-44a0-880b-dd6b8a904179"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of Geospatial Data Loading","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747270","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The recent explosion in the number and size of spatial remote sensing datasets from satellite missions creates new opportunities for data-driven approaches in domains such as climate change monitoring and disaster management. These approaches typically involve a feature engineering step that summarizes remote sensing pixel data located within zones of interest defined by another spatial dataset, an operation called zonal statistics. Although several spatial systems support zonal statistics operations, they differ significantly in terms of interfaces, architectures, and algorithms, making it hard for users to select the best system for a specific workload. To address this limitation, we propose Raven, a zonal statistics framework that provides users with a unified interface across multiple execution backends, while facilitating easy benchmarking and comparisons across systems. This demonstration showcases Raven 's multi-backend execution environment, domain-specific declarative language, optimization techniques, and benchmarking capabilities.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dusella, Gereon","Gavriilidis, Haralampos","Nuhu, Laert","Markl, Volker","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747237"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deutsche Kreditbank AG","German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","Technical University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Big spatial data","Earth observation","Satellite imagery","Spatial join","parcel based classification","unified spatial data analytics","zonal statistics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi backend zonal statistics execution with raven","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3626246.3654730","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747237","identifier":[{"id":"85196363917","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-794a1826-1cdb-4657-862b-ef8d20b623d2"],"keyword":["big spatial data","earth observation","parcel-based classification","satellite imagery","spatial join","unified spatial data analytics","zonal statistics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CF504FDB9D4613DEFA4BCFD0977153F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3626246.3654730","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"deutsche kreditbank ag","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Deutsche Kreditbank AG","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german research center for artificial intelligence","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gereon","key":"dusellapau","last":"Dusella","name":"Dusella, Gereon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haralampos","key":"gavriilidispau","last":"Gavriilidis","name":"Gavriilidis, Haralampos","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laert","key":"nuhupau","last":"Nuhu","name":"Nuhu, Laert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3626246.3654730","isbn":["9798400704222"],"pages":"532-535","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"SIGMOD/PODS '24","status":"p","title":"Companion of the 2024 International Conference on Management of Data"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196363917"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-794a1826-1cdb-4657-862b-ef8d20b623d2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-Backend Zonal Statistics Execution with Raven","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747237","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Spatial join processing techniques that identify intersections between complex geometries (e.g., polygons) commonly follow a two-step filter-and-refine pipeline. The filter step evaluates the query predicate on the minimum bounding rectangles (MBRs) of the geometries, while the refinement step eliminates false positives by applying the query on the exact geometries. To accelerate spatial join evaluation over complex geometries, we propose a raster intervals approximation of object geometries and introduce a powerful intermediate step in the pipeline. In a preprocessing phase, our method (i) rasterizes each object geometry using a fine grid, (ii) models groups of nearby cells that intersect the polygon as an interval, and (iii) encodes each interval with a bit string capturing the overlap of each cell in it with the polygon. Going one step further, we improve our approach by approximating each object with two sets of intervals that succinctly capture the raster cells that (i) intersect with the object and (ii) are fully contained within the object. Using this representation, we show that we can verify whether two polygons intersect through a sequence of linear-time joins between the interval sets. Our approximations are effectively compressible and customizable for partitioned data and polygons of varying sizes, rasterized at different granularities. Finally, we propose a novel algorithm that computes the interval approximation of a polygon without fully rasterizing it first, rendering the computation of approximations orders of magnitude faster. Experiments on real data demonstrate the effectiveness and efficiency of our proposal over previous work.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Georgiadis, Thanasis","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Mamoulis, Nikos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789573"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Greece"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Ioannina"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"raster interval object approximations for spatial intersection joins","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00778-024-00887-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789573","identifier":[{"id":"85212083745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c8f53119-39c1-4b90-be0a-2c1e513058d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1F6C2A343DAE1AF75B2000A6E69DECC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00778-024-00887-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00778-024-00887-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gr","key":"university of ioannina","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Ioannina","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thanasis","key":"georgiadispau","last":"Georgiadis","name":"Georgiadis, Thanasis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikos","key":"mamoulispau","last":"Mamoulis","name":"Mamoulis, Nikos","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00778-024-00887-4","issn":["0949877X","10668888"],"issn_org":["10668888"],"issue":"1","journal":"VLDB Journal","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"VLDB Journal","title_org":"The VLDB Journal","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212083745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c8f53119-39c1-4b90-be0a-2c1e513058d4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Raster interval object approximations for spatial intersection joins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789573","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"A recent trend in stream processing is offloading the computation of decomposable aggregation functions (DAF) from cloud nodes to geo-distributed fog/edge devices to decrease latency and improve energy efficiency. However, deploying DAFs on low-end devices is challenging due to their volatility and limited resources. Additionally, in geo-distributed fog/edge environments, creating new operator instances on demand and replicating operators ubiquitously is restricted, posing challenges for achieving load balancing without overloading devices. Existing work predominantly focuses on cloud environments, overlooking DAF operator placement in resource-constrained and unreliable geo-distributed settings. This paper presents NEMO, a resource-aware optimization approach that determines the replication factor and placement of DAF operators in resource-constrained geo-distributed topologies. Leveraging Euclidean embeddings of network topologies and a set of heuristics, NEMO scales to millions of nodes and handles topological changes through adaptive re-placement and re-replication decisions. Compared to existing solutions, NEMO achieves up to 6× lower latency and up to 15× reduction in communication cost, while preventing overloaded nodes. Moreover, NEMO re-optimizes placements in constant time, regardless of the topology size. As a result, it lays the foundation to efficiently process continuous data streams on large, heterogeneous, and geo-distributed topologies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Chatziliadis, Xenofon","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Eracar, Alphan","Zeuch, Steffen","Markl, Volker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730164"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","Technical University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Decomposable Aggregation Functions","Fog Edge Computing","Geo distributed Topologies","Resource aware Optimization","Stream processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient placement of decomposable aggregation functions for stream processing over large geo distributed topologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol17/p1501-chatziliadis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730164","identifier":[{"id":"85190643150","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-35fbea3a-a59b-47c7-872b-4a162b00e617"],"keyword":["Decomposable Aggregation Functions","Fog/Edge Computing","Geo-distributed Topologies","Resource-aware Optimization","Stream Processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5961B53BD698C111D2626B5EC1A01272"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.vldb.org/pvldb/vol17/p1501-chatziliadis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german research center for artificial intelligence","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"chatziliadispau","last":"Chatziliadis","name":"Chatziliadis, Xenofon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni","key":"tziritazacharatoupau","last":"Tzirita Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","name_org":"Tzirita Zacharatou, Eleni","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alphan","key":"eracarpau","last":"Eracar","name":"Eracar, Alphan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"zeuchpau","last":"Zeuch","name":"Zeuch, Steffen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21508097"],"issue":"6","journal":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","pages":"1501-1514","publisher":"VLDB Endowment","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190643150"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-35fbea3a-a59b-47c7-872b-4a162b00e617"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficient Placement of Decomposable Aggregation Functions for Stream Processing over Large Geo-Distributed Topologies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730164","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Spreadsheets are widely used for data exploration. Since spreadsheet systems have limited capabilities, users often need to load spreadsheets to other data science environments to perform advanced analytics. However, current approaches for spreadsheet loading suffer from either high runtime or memory usage, which hinders data exploration on commodity systems. To make spreadsheet loading practical on commodity systems, we introduce a novel parser that minimizes memory usage by tightly coupling decompression and parsing. Furthermore, to reduce the runtime, we introduce optimized spreadsheet-specific parsing routines and employ parallelism. To evaluate our approach, we implement prototypes for loading Excel spreadsheets into R and Python environments. Our evaluation shows that our novel approach is up to 3× faster while consuming up to 40× less memory than state-of-the-art approaches.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gavriilidis, Haralampos","Henze, Felix","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Markl, Volker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384328"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["Access Microfinance Holding AG","All Global Affiliations","German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","Technical University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Data loading","Parsing parallelization","Spreadsheet parser"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sheetreader efficient specialized spreadsheet parsing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95293524/gavriilidis_et_al.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384328","identifier":[{"id":"85148048140","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d0702053-353a-4f38-8505-0cc61916219a"],"keyword":["Data loading","Parsing parallelization","Spreadsheet parser"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A926DB9E848E651F2D83654EA05A983"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95293524/gavriilidis_et_al.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"access microfinance holding ag","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Access Microfinance Holding AG","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"german research center for artificial intelligence","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haralampos","key":"gavriilidispau","last":"Gavriilidis","name":"Gavriilidis, Haralampos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"henzepau","last":"Henze","name":"Henze, Felix","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.is.2023.102183","issn":["03064379","18736076"],"issn_org":["03064379"],"journal":"Information Systems","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information Systems","volume":"115"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148048140"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d0702053-353a-4f38-8505-0cc61916219a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SheetReader: Efficient Specialized Spreadsheet Parsing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384328","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Sketches are a popular approximation technique for large datasets and high-velocity data streams. While custom FPGA-based hardware has shown admirable throughput at sketching, the state-of-the-art exploits data parallelism by fully replicating resources and constructing independent summaries for every parallel input value. We consider this approach pessimistic, as it guarantees constant processing rates by provisioning resources for the worst case. We propose a novel optimistic sketching architecture for FPGAs that partitions a single sketch into multiple independent banks shared among all input values, thus significantly reducing resource consumption. However, skewed input data distributions can result in conflicting accesses to banks and impair the processing rate. To mitigate the effect of skew, we add mergers that exploit temporal locality by combining recent updates. Our evaluation shows that an optimistic architecture is feasible and reduces the utilization of critical FPGA resources proportionally to the number of parallel input values. We further show that FPGA accelerators provide up to 2.6x higher throughput than a recent CPU and GPU, while larger sketch sizes enabled by optimistic architectures improve accuracy by up to an order of magnitude in a realistic sketching application.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kiefer, Martin","Poulakis, Ilias","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Markl, Volker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384513"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Data parallelism","FPGA sketching","High throughput computing","Resource optimization","Temporal locality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimistic data parallelism for fpga accelerated sketching","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.14778/3579075.3579085","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384513","identifier":[{"id":"85149914442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-dcbf8603-1ba5-4a72-b58b-8d469cb15c03"],"keyword":["Data parallelism","FPGA sketching","High-throughput computing","Resource optimization","Temporal locality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F36D66FFC878371DEE1DC4DD47193190"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95292336/p1113_kiefer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.14778/3579075.3579085","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"kieferpau","last":"Kiefer","name":"Kiefer, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ilias","key":"poulakispau","last":"Poulakis","name":"Poulakis, Ilias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14778/3579075.3579085","issn":["21508097"],"issue":"5","journal":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","publisher":"VLDB Endowment","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149914442"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dcbf8603-1ba5-4a72-b58b-8d469cb15c03"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Optimistic Data Parallelism for FPGA-Accelerated Sketching","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384513","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Spatial data is ubiquitous. Massive amounts of data are generated every day from a plethora of sources such as billions of GPS-enabled devices (e.g., cell phones, cars, and sensors), consumer-based applications (e.g., Uber and Strava), and social media platforms (e.g., location-tagged posts on Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram). This exponential growth in spatial data has led the research community to build systems and applications for efficient spatial data processing. In this study, we apply a recently developed machine-learned search technique for single-dimensional sorted data to spatial indexing. Specifically, we partition spatial data using six traditional spatial partitioning techniques and employ machine-learned search within each partition to support point, range, distance, and spatial join queries. Adhering to the latest research trends, we tune the partitioning techniques to be instance-optimized. By tuning each partitioning technique for optimal performance, we demonstrate that: (i) grid-based index structures outperform tree-based index structures (from 1.23× to 2.47×), (ii) learning-enhanced variants of commonly used spatial index structures outperform their original counterparts (from 1.44× to 53.34× faster), (iii) machine-learned search within a partition is faster than binary search by 11.79% - 39.51% when filtering on one dimension, (iv) the benefit of machine-learned search diminishes in the presence of other compute-intensive operations (e.g. scan costs in higher selectivity queries, Haversine distance computation, and point-in-polygon tests), and (v) index lookup is the bottleneck for tree-based structures, which could potentially be reduced by linearizing the indexed partitions. Additional Key Words and Phrases: spatial data, indexing, machine-learning, spatial queries, geospatial","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pandey, Varun","Van Renen, Alexander","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Kipf, Andreas","Sabek, Ibrahim","Ding, Jialin","Markl, Volker","Kemper, Alfons"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695234"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amazon Web Services","Technical University of Berlin","Technical University of Munich","University of Southern California"],"keyword":["Geospatial","Indexing","Machine learning","Spatial data","spatial queries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing in memory spatial indexing with learned search","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2309.06354","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-695234","ids":["itu-3eb11570-f1f4-45a3-9552-17ea3d73e12b"],"keyword":["geospatial","indexing","machine-learning","spatial data","spatial queries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-718FF3FC3CB71A2B91651AA31804F150"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101958215/2309.06354.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2309.06354","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"amazon web services","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Amazon Web Services","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of southern california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Southern California","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Varun","key":"pandeypau","last":"Pandey","name":"Pandey, Varun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"vanrenenpau","last":"Van Renen","name":"Van Renen, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"kipfpau","last":"Kipf","name":"Kipf, Andreas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ibrahim","key":"sabekpau","last":"Sabek","name":"Sabek, Ibrahim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jialin","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Jialin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfons","key":"kemperpau","last":"Kemper","name":"Kemper, Alfons","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2309.06354","pages":"26","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3eb11570-f1f4-45a3-9552-17ea3d73e12b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhancing In-Memory Spatial Indexing with Learned Search","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695234","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Burrell, David","Chatziliadis, Xenofon","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Zeuch, Steffen","Markl, Volker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383715"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","Technical University of Berlin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"workload prediction for iot data management systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18420/BTW2023-64","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383715","identifier":[{"id":"85149958114","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a803feba-0303-4f29-bcbf-fe354434f7aa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-643C14CA7BD8358FB5A112F8A0F98CD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95294585/C3_04.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18420/BTW2023-64","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german research center for artificial intelligence","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"burrellpau","last":"Burrell","name":"Burrell, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"chatziliadispau","last":"Chatziliadis","name":"Chatziliadis, Xenofon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"zeuchpau","last":"Zeuch","name":"Zeuch, Steffen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"marklpau","last":"Markl","name":"Markl, Volker","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18420/btw2023-64","publisher":"Gesellschaft für Informatik","status":"p","title":"Datenbanksysteme für Business, Technologie und Web (BTW 2023), 20. Fachtagung des GI-Fachbereichs „Datenbanken und Informationssysteme\" (DBIS), 06.-10, März 2023, Dresden, Germany, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149958114"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a803feba-0303-4f29-bcbf-fe354434f7aa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Workload Prediction for IoT Data Management Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383715","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The spatial intersection join an important spatial query operation, due to its popularity and high complexity. The spatial join pipeline takes as input two collections of spatial objects (e.g., polygons). In the filter step, pairs of object MBRs that intersect are identified and passed to the refinement step for verification of the join predicate on the exact object geometries. The bottleneck of spatial join evaluation is in the refinement step. We introduce APRIL, a powerful intermediate step in the pipeline, which is based on raster interval approximations of object geometries. Our technique applies a sequence of interval joins on 'intervalized' object approximations to determine whether the objects intersect or not. Compared to previous work, APRIL approximations are simpler, occupy much less space, and achieve similar pruning effectiveness at a much higher speed. Besides intersection joins between polygons, APRIL can directly be applied and has high effectiveness for polygonal range queries, within joins, and polygon-linestring joins. By applying a lightweight compression technique, APRIL approximations may occupy even less space than object MBRs. Furthermore, APRIL can be customized to apply on partitioned data and on polygons of varying sizes, rasterized at different granularities. Our last contribution is a novel algorithm that computes the APRIL approximation of a polygon without having to rasterize it in full, which is orders of magnitude faster than the computation of other raster approximations. Experiments on real data demonstrate the effectiveness and efficiency of APRIL; compared to the state-of-the-art intermediate filter, APRIL occupies 2x-8x less space, is 3.5x-8.5x more time-efficient, and reduces the end-to-end join cost up to 3 times.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Georgiadis, Thanasis","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Mamoulis, Nikos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695275"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Greece"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Ioannina"],"keyword":["Geometric pruning","Polygon intersection","Raster interval approximation","Spatial join","Spatial query optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"april approximating polygons as raster interval lists","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2307.01716","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-695275","ids":["itu-a6d95b38-963b-41c4-9f54-bfae6d01948a"],"keyword":["Geometric pruning","Polygon intersection","Raster interval approximation","Spatial join","Spatial query optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-42F00F0D5CE90FFD4EA75FD6B5FEE41C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.01716","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2307.01716","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gr","key":"university of ioannina","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Ioannina","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thanasis","key":"georgiadispau","last":"Georgiadis","name":"Georgiadis, Thanasis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":"3ec363e3-83f0-4dd8-9b2d-b87a7d34dc55","name":"Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","orcid":"0000-0001-8873-5455","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikos","key":"mamoulispau","last":"Mamoulis","name":"Mamoulis, Nikos","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2307.01716","pages":"12","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a6d95b38-963b-41c4-9f54-bfae6d01948a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"APRIL: Approximating Polygons as Raster Interval Lists","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695275","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In the 38th IEEE International Conference on Data Engineering (ICDE), 2022, panel discussions were introduced after paper presentations to facilitate in-depth exploration of research topics and encourage participation. These discussions, enriched by diverse perspectives from experts and active audience involvement, provided fresh insights and a broader understanding of each topic. The introduction of panel discussions exceeded expectations, attracting a larger number of participants to the virtual sessions. This article summarizes the virtual panels held during ICDE’22, focusing on sessions such as Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery, Federated Learning, Graph Data Management, Graph Neural Networks, Spatial and Temporal Data Management, and Spatial and Temporal Data Mining. By showcasing the success of panel discussions in generating inspiring discussions and promoting participation, this article aims to benefit the data engineering community, providing a valuable resource for researchers and suggesting a compelling format of holding research sessions for future conferences.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Bao, Zhifeng","Bouros, Panagiotis","Cheng, Reynold","Choi, Byron","Dignös, Anton","Ding, Wei","Fang, Yixiang","Han, Boyang","Hu, Jilin","Khan, Arijit","Lin, Wenqing","Lin, Xuemin","Long, Cheng","Mamoulis, Nikos","Pei, Jian","Renz, Matthias","Shekhar, Shashi","Shi, Jieming","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Wang, Sibo","Wang, Xiao","Wang, Xue","Chi-Wing Wong, Raymond","Yan, Da","Yan, Xifeng","Yang, Bin","Yao, Dezhong","Zhang, Ce","Zhao, Peilin","Zhu, Rong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718883"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","China","Germany","Greece","Hong Kong","Italy","Singapore","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["Alibaba Group","All Globa