{"abstract":"The rapid increase of traffic data generated by different sensing systems opens many opportunities to improve transportation services. An important opportunity is to enable stochastic routing that computes the arrival time probabilities for each suggested route instead of only the expected travel time. However, traffic datasets typically have many missing values, which prevents the construction of stochastic speeds. To address this limitation, we propose the Stochastic Spatio-Temporal Graph Convolutional Network (SST-GCN) architecture that accurately imputes missing speed distributions in a road network. SST-GCN combines Temporal Convolutional Networks and Graph Convolutional Networks into a single framework to capture both spatial and temporal correlations between road segments and time intervals. Moreover, to cope with datasets with many missing values, we propose a novel self-adaptive contextaware diffusion process that regulates the propagated information around the network, avoiding the spread of false information. We extensively evaluate the effectiveness of SST-GCN on real-world datasets, showing that it achieves from 4.6% to 50% higher accuracy than state-of-the-art baselines using three different evaluation metrics. Furthermore, multiple ablation studies confirm our design choices and scalability to large road networks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Muniz Cuza, Carlos E.","Ho, Nguyen","Zacharatou, Eleni Tzirita","Bach Pedersen, Torben","Yang, Bin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384917"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Missing Data Imputation","Self Adaptive Diffusion","Spatio Temporal Graph Convolutional Networks","Stochastic Routing","Traffic data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatio temporal graph convolutional network for stochastic traffic speed imputation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90405525/paper_42_sigspatial_2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384917","ids":["itu-f7c050ab-171b-4e12-b4ed-e019cd17b339"],"keyword":["Missing Data Imputation","Self-Adaptive Diffusion","Spatio-Temporal Graph Convolutional Networks","Stochastic Routing","Traffic Data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9C68A741822F9D3D999D6353FC970A81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90405525/paper_42_sigspatial_2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos E.","key":"munizcuzapau","last":"Muniz Cuza","name":"Muniz Cuza, Carlos E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nguyen","key":"hopau","last":"Ho","name":"Ho, Nguyen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni Tzirita","key":"zacharatoupau","last":"Zacharatou","locid":